- Aditya Verma — 20251651009
- Pratik Sinha — 20251651071

## Project Overview

The Disaster Resource Coordination Platform is a web services project designed to support disaster response, shelter management, field reporting, and emergency resource coordination. It demonstrates REST APIs, GraphQL interfaces, service integration, external SOAP/WSDL communication, request validation, service contracts, authentication, and error handling.

The platform consists of six logically separated services: Shelter & Inventory Service, Field Report Service, Resource Request & Transfer Service, Disaster Alert Integration Service, Identity & Access Service, and API & Coordination Query Service.

The frontend uses React.js, while the backend uses Node.js and Express.js. PostgreSQL is used for data storage. The platform supports shelter registration and search, inventory management, field report submission, resource requests and approvals, disaster alert retrieval, and role-based access control.

This project focuses on defining clear service boundaries, documenting service contracts, managing data ownership, and enabling reliable communication between services during disaster response operations.

---

# Task 1: System Capabilities

The Disaster Resource Coordination Platform provides the following capabilities to support shelter management, disaster reporting, and emergency resource coordination.

| ID | Capability | Description |
|---|---|---|
| C1 | **Register Shelters** | Allows Coordinators and Administrators to register shelters with their location, capacity, and contact details. |
| C2 | **Manage Inventory** | Allows Shelter Staff to update and track available food, water, medicine, beds, and blankets. |
| C3 | **Submit Field Reports** | Allows field personnel to submit situation reports and photo metadata, even when network connectivity is unreliable. |
| C4 | **Request Resources** | Allows Shelter Staff to request resources by specifying the resource type, required quantity, and urgency. |
| C5 | **Approve Resource Transfers** | Allows Coordinators to approve, deny, or fulfill resource-transfer requests while preventing duplicate approvals. |
| C6 | **Retrieve Disaster Alerts** | Retrieves disaster declarations and weather alerts from an external government SOAP/WSDL service. |
| C7 | **Monitor Shelter Status** | Allows Coordinators to view aggregated shelter status, inventory information, and recent field reports. |
| C8 | **Search Shelters** | Allows users to find shelters using location, shelter status, and resource availability filters. |
| C9 | **Authenticate Users** | Verifies user identities using JWT-based authentication and manages role-based access permissions. |
| C10 | **Expose Data Through APIs** | Provides shelter, inventory, report, resource-request, and alert information through REST and GraphQL interfaces. |
| C11 | **Control API Traffic** | Applies configurable rate limits and returns appropriate responses when clients exceed their limits. |
| C12 | **Audit and Trace Operations** | Maintains relevant audit records and structured logs using correlation IDs to support traceability and troubleshooting. |

## Summary

These capabilities describe the major jobs performed by the Disaster Resource Coordination Platform. They cover shelter and inventory management, field reporting, resource coordination, disaster-alert integration, data access, security, and operational monitoring.

